  <HOMEWORK title="DDR Bring-Up 4: Train CS/CA timing next" prompt="ZQ cal is clean now. The memory test still fails almost every read with a timeout, even though CK, the command bus, and chip-select all look completely normal on a scope. Writes seem to go through. What training step runs right after ZQ cal, and is it done yet?"
            hint="CS/CA training aligns *when* this chip samples chip-select against the rest of the command bus - it isn't automatic after reset. Check this chip's own CS timing-error setting."
            explanation="CS/CA training was simply never run: this chip's own chip-select sampling lags the real signal by most of a unit interval. A read is only asserted for a single unit interval before the controller moves on, so by the time this chip's own &quot;am I selected&quot; check catches up, the window has already closed - it misses the read outright and the controller eventually times out. Writes still work because a write burst holds CS asserted continuously across many consecutive unit intervals, so a timing lag that would miss one brief pulse doesn't matter once CS has been high for a while. Run CS/CA training (bring the CS timing error back to 0) before moving on to the write-path training steps - the identical real symptom as DDR Homework 6 in the flat set."/>
</LABCHAIN>
